A goal file that links into a --deny-dir directory no longer reaches the model. Before this fix, the secret went into the system prompt even under --safe-mode. Committed as a39737e0 with Part of #1002; build, test, clippy and fmt all pass.

Before and after. Test setup: proj/.yoyo/goal.md is a symlink to secret/goal.md, which contains GOAL_SECRET_QQ7. I ran yoyo --print-system-prompt from proj and counted that token:

| flags | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| --deny-dir secret | 1 | 0 |
| --deny-dir secret --safe-mode | 1 | 0 |
| --allow-dir proj (link target outside it) | 1 | 0 |
| --allow-dir proj --allow-dir secret | — | 1 (target allowed, still loads) |
| no flags | 1 | 1, no warning |

What changed:
• **Which reads are gated:** five places read the goal file. Two of them send it to the model, and both are now gated:
  • the `# Current Goal block in the system prompt (cli.rs`)
  • the /goal check prompt
  
  The other three (/goal show, the goal line in /status, the startup tip) only print to the user's own terminal, so I left them alone.
• **How:** before reading the file, it calls `DirectoryRestrictions::check_path`, the same check `read_file` uses, so a link is judged by where it points. Task 1 didn't add a shared helper, so I called that check directly rather than writing a new one.
• **Caller safety:** goal_for_prompt now requires the restrictions as an argument, so any future caller that leaves them out won't compile.
• **/goal check:** when the file is refused, it now says so instead of the misleading "No goal set". The warning prints at normal volume, with display-safe text and no symbols in plain mode.
• **Fourth file:** the task allowed three source files, and I touched a fourth: a one-line change in `commands.rs`. Clippy failed until the old `handle_goal` re-export was switched to the new fenced version.

Testing: 7 new Unix tests, including one confirming that a normal goal file with no restrictions comes through byte-for-byte unchanged. As a check, I disabled the fence in one combined break-run-restore command. Exactly the three refusal tests failed, and all passed again once it was restored.

Docs: dated note added to the commands_goal.rs entry in ARCHITECTURE.md, and one paragraph added to docs/src/configuration/permissions.md.

Left open on purpose:
• **--safe-mode:** with no directory flags it still loads the goal file (count 1), while it skips `CLAUDE.md` (count 0). Whether safe-mode should skip the goal too is a design question I didn't settle. I posted the readings and the question on #1002 and confirmed the comment shows up with gh issue view.
• **`--restricted:** it adds the current folder to the allow list *after* the goal is loaded, so that limit doesn't apply to the goal file. Only the user's own --allow-dir/--deny-dir` do. I recorded this in ARCHITECTURE.md and the issue comment but didn't change it.
• **Rest of #1002:** I haven't checked `memory.json`, skills, or the repo map yet.
